"informations\"\u003e1255×856 63.4 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/6/f/6f0c4adeae4ed2b44e69cbfad073560ff7e9d75b.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/fQnkOpr7IOTJk1iVPCRPy2ZOFMn.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot From 2026-09-11 19-13-43\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/6/f/6f0c4adeae4ed2b44e69cbfad073560ff7e9d75b_2_690x427.png\" alt=\"Screenshot From 2026-09-11 19-13-43\" data-base62-sha1=\"fQnkOpr7IOTJk1iVPCRPy2ZOFMn\" width=\"690\" height=\"427\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/6/f/6f0c4adeae4ed2b44e69cbfad073560ff7e9d75b_2_690x427.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/6/f/6f0c4adeae4ed2b44e69cbfad073560ff7e9d75b_2_1035x640.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/6/f/6f0c4adeae4ed2b44e69cbfad073560ff7e9d75b.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"1A1A1B\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot From 2026-09-11 19-13-43\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1377×854 64.5 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eand before first update, everything was fine , same network , no changes !\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-11T19:21:35.193Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":6.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171376,"topic_slug":"cant-login-after-updating","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":62449,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/cant-login-after-updating/171376/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":489421,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-12T09:06:33.973Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report and the new screenshots. They give an important clue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe diagnostics didn’t fail completely. Green checks (passing) are DNS, Authentication UI, Cursor Tab, and Agent Endpoint. Red checks with \u003ccode\u003eFailed to fetch\u003c/code\u003e are Marketplace, \u003ccode\u003eAuthentication\u003c/code\u003e (this is a separate check, not the same as \u003ccode\u003eAuthentication UI\u003c/code\u003e), Downloads, and CDN. So your machine can reach some of our domains, but not others. The IDE login is most likely failing because the \u003ccode\u003eAuthentication\u003c/code\u003e check is failing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis kind of partial result usually points to an issue with specific domains, like network, DNS, proxy, firewall, or SSL inspection, not a full network outage. A terminal \u003ccode\u003ecurl\u003c/code\u003e test can show if an endpoint is reachable outside Cursor, but it doesn’t prove the full app authentication flow will work. If you’re using a proxy, also try Cursor in HTTP/1.1 mode and fully restart the app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere’s what to check in order. Please tell me at which step anything changes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf you have a VPN, a per app firewall (OpenSnitch, Portmaster, etc), or an allowed apps list or split tunneling, temporarily disable it (or test on a phone hotspot), then fully quit and reopen Cursor and click Log In. If your firewall uses per application rules, check if there’s a separate allow rule for the new Cursor binary (after updates the file changes).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor Settings \u0026gt; Network \u0026gt; Required Domains \u0026gt; Copy Domains, then add those domains to the allowlist in your firewall, proxy, or VPN. Main groups are \u003ccode\u003e*.cursor.sh\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e*.cursor-cdn.com\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorapi.com\u003c/code\u003e (and for Grok Bot also \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e*.*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor Settings \u0026gt; Network \u0026gt; HTTP Compatibility Mode \u0026gt; switch to HTTP/1.1, fully restart Cursor, then run Network Diagnostics again. In proxy setups, some transport paths can fail even if some services work.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn your terminal, run this and tell me what status code you get:\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003ecurl -sS -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" \"https://api2.cursor.sh/auth/poll?uuid=test\u0026amp;verifier=test\"\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003e404\u003c/code\u003e is a useful sign that the endpoint is reachable from the terminal, but it still doesn’t prove the full auth flow works in the app. If \u003ccode\u003ecurl\u003c/code\u003e fails completely, your VPN or network is blocking it.\u003cbr\u003e\n5. Let me know how you installed Cursor on Arch (AUR package, AppImage, or something else) and whether the email in the IDE matches your forum email.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReference for network diagnostics:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/help/troubleshooting/network\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003ehttps://cursor.com/help/troubleshooting/network\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-12T09:13:36.484Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":6.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171376,"topic_slug":"cant-login-after-updating","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://cursor.com/help/troubleshooting/network","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Network, proxy, and remote connections | Cursor Docs","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/cant-login-after-updating/171376/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":489437,"name":"","username":"Em_Strange","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/ebca7d/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-12T09:37:22.039Z","cooked":"\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003e\u0026gt; curl -sS -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" \"https://api2.cursor.sh/auth/poll?uuid=test\u0026amp;verifier=test\"                           \n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e404\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ei do use vpn and portmaster , but have used it with cursor for years now , because i have cursor excluded from both the vpn and portmaster . i even have now tested with complete shutdown of portmaster and vpn , issue persist , with the 3.19 i can login , from 3.20.10 or the new .17 issue persist .\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003erebooted system , router etc , everything else works perfectly except cursor 3.20 above\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/c/f/cf5354eb899dc33257e04fb742718ea2bc10f1ee.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/tA5naLgOYNoVtStezQIG2cDJX8a.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot From 2026-09-12 09-37-08\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/c/f/cf5354eb899dc33257e04fb742718ea2bc10f1ee_2_660x500.png\" alt=\"Screenshot From 2026-09-12 09-37-08\" data-base62-sha1=\"tA5naLgOYNoVtStezQIG2cDJX8a\" width=\"660\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/c/f/cf5354eb899dc33257e04fb742718ea2bc10f1ee_2_660x500.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/c/f/cf5354eb899dc33257e04fb742718ea2bc10f1ee_2_990x750.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/c/f/cf5354eb899dc33257e04fb742718ea2bc10f1ee.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"201F20\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot From 2026-09-12 09-37-08\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1112×842 61.4 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-12T09:37:22.039Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":6.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171376,"topic_slug":"cant-login-after-updating","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":62449,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/cant-login-after-updating/171376/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":489495,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-12T11:58:19.314Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for the detailed test. The \u003ccode\u003ecurl\u003c/code\u003e with \u003ccode\u003e404\u003c/code\u003e plus \u003ccode\u003eread ECONNRESET\u003c/code\u003e in Diagnostics is exactly what helps narrow this down. From your screenshot I see DNS, Authentication UI, Cursor Tab, and Agent Endpoint are green, but HTTP/2, SSL, API, Ping, Chat, and Agent fail with \u003ccode\u003eread ECONNRESET\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA \u003ccode\u003e404\u003c/code\u003e from \u003ccode\u003ecurl\u003c/code\u003e means your machine can reach us. But the app itself gets \u003ccode\u003eECONNRESET\u003c/code\u003e connection reset on encrypted channels. A reset that hits the app but not \u003ccode\u003ecurl\u003c/code\u003e usually means something is breaking the app’s encrypted or HTTP/2 connections. The two most common causes are a local app firewall like Portmaster, especially after an update when the binary changed, and a network or proxy that doesn’t handle HTTP/2 well. In that case \u003ccode\u003ecurl\u003c/code\u003e works, but Cursor’s gRPC streams don’t.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst, a quick HTTP/2 test:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor Settings \u0026gt; Network \u0026gt; HTTP Compatibility Mode \u0026gt; switch to \u003ccode\u003eHTTP/1.1\u003c/code\u003e, fully restart Cursor, then run Diagnostics again. If \u003ccode\u003eECONNRESET\u003c/code\u003e goes away on HTTP/1.1, it’s a network or proxy issue, not Portmaster.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf that doesn’t help, let’s check Portmaster. Two important details:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClosing Portmaster from the tray or UI does not stop it. The core service \u003ccode\u003eportmaster-core\u003c/code\u003e keeps running as a system service and filters at the kernel level. To actually disable it for a test run:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003esudo systemctl stop portmaster\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you have a separate Portmaster DNS service, stop that too. Then fully quit Cursor and open it again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn update replaces the Cursor binary. Your old Portmaster exception and any VPN split tunnel are tied to the old file and won’t match the new 3.20 binary, so the new binary can be treated as unknown and blocked even if it looks like an exception exists. That matches what you’re seeing, DNS is green but TLS connections fail.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat to check:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Portmaster, open Network Monitor and find the Cursor process. Check if it has blocked connections. Look for a gray bar or red dot and Applied Setting. If yes, set it to Allow or create a fresh allow rule for the new 3.20 binary.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Terminal run \u003ccode\u003eenv | grep -i proxy\u003c/code\u003e and tell me if it prints anything.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Cursor Settings, find \u003ccode\u003eHttp: Proxy Support\u003c/code\u003e, set it to \u003ccode\u003eon\u003c/code\u003e, then fully restart Cursor.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMain confirmation step: if you fully stop the Portmaster service using \u003ccode\u003esystemctl\u003c/code\u003e, not just closing the window, and also disable VPN, then try HTTP/1.1, and the problem still stays, tell me. That changes the picture and then we’ll dig deeper with logs.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-12T11:58:19.314Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":1.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171376,"topic_slug":"cant-login-after-updating","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":62449,"username":"Em_Strange","name":"","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/ebca7d/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/cant-login-after-updating/171376/8","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[489158,489210,489421,489437,489495]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":284,"name":"installation","slug":"installation"},{"id":305,"name":"login","slug":"login"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Can\u0026rsquo;t login after updating","id":171376,"title":"Can't login after updating","posts_count":5,"created_at":"2026-09-11T18:05:38.125Z","views":49,"reply_count":2,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-12T11:58:19.314Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"cant-login-after-updating","category_id":6,"word_count":1180,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":62449,"featured_link":null,"pinned_globally":false,"pinned_at":null,"pinned_until":null,"image_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/a/2/a2bb82dec78290c8e13dd55e3128065939177e7e_2_1024x775.png","slow_mode_seconds":0,"draft":null,"draft_key":"topic_171376","draft_sequence":null,"unpinned":null,"pinned":false,"current_post_number":1,"highest_post_number":8,"deleted_by":null,"actions_summary":[{"id":4,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":8,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":10,"count":